6048915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1031 "Analyzing and Interpreting Graphs of Linear Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1033 1588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050112 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "2df5c93f-1787-57c4-a96b-9af6f2216425" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138211 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1526" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138211 #edb/ref 1071 "Density $D$ is the rate that mass $M$ changes as volume $V$ changes. What are the units of density in terms of base units?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138211 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0782388-8184-5922-8e9e-d9edcf727264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138211 #edb/ref 1074 "We *measure the change* in the mass, as *we change* the volume. Consequently, any appropriate unit must take the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{unit of mass}}{\\textrm{unit of volume}}.\n$$\n\nThe base unit for mass is $\\textrm{kg},$ and the base unit for volume is $\\textrm{m}^3.$ Therefore, the units of density are\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{kg}}{\\textrm{m}^3},\n$$\n\nor, kilograms per cubic meter." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138313 #edb/ref 1069 "e-901" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138313 #edb/ref 1071 "A tank is being filled with water. What is an appropriate unit for measuring the rate of change of water volume in the tank, as time goes on?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138313 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66c31f3c-2abb-51ff-b8d5-8377aeb90d80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138313 #edb/ref 1074 "We *measure the change* of the volume as *we change* the amount of time. Consequently, any appropriate unit for measuring the rate of change of water volume in the tank must take the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{unit of volume}}{\\textrm{unit of time}}.\n$$\n\nSome examples of appropriate units include $\\dfrac{\\textrm{liters}}{\\textrm{hour}},$ $\\dfrac{\\textrm{m}^3}{\\textrm{min}},$ and $\\dfrac{\\textrm{cm}^3}{\\textrm{s}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138440 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138440 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186138794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138440 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186138819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138440 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138440 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138440 #edb/ref 1039 "Choosing Appropriate Units When Base Units Are Not Required" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138440 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186138313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138440 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "86db8dde-c4ad-5ba3-9022-afe85acbc3d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138458 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138458 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138458 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138458 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138458 #edb/ref 1039 "Choosing Appropriate Units When Base Units Are Required" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138458 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186138211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138458 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "010539bb-ae6a-5071-a7bd-25c40d5a9717" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186139371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186139372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186139408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1045 "Selecting Units for Rates of Change" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186139371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138591 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ddf9f6c0-2c82-5508-b796-5212ce1fc527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139371 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186139372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139371 #edb/ref 1061 3029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139371 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "81f48e8d-1f8d-5602-aaa8-6dbfe592f877" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139371 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186139598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139372 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186139408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139372 #edb/ref 1061 3033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139372 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fc01ce33-f078-54a8-aba9-533e122ac058" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139372 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186138440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139408 #edb/ref 1061 4786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139408 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "224fd6c9-017e-5d25-880a-8e0f92b408fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139408 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186138458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139598 #edb/ref 1064 "Sometimes, when we are choosing an appropriate unit, we are not given any formula to use. \n\nThis often occurs when we measure the **rate of change** of something. A rate of change measures how much something changes as we change something else.\n\nIn such cases, we can use a quotient to work out an appropriate unit. The numerator is what we measure the change of, and the denominator is what we change:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}\\textrm{what we measure the change of}}{\\color{red}\\textrm{what we change}}\n$$\n\nFor instance, suppose that a newly opened store wants to measure the rate at which the number of customers increases each day.\n\nWe *measure the change* of the number of customers, as *we change* the number of days, so the most appropriate unit is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}\\textrm{customers}}{\\color{red}\\textrm{day}},\n$$\n\nor, customers per day." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139598 #edb/ref 1065 1401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139598 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "56217ef8-a09e-5cdd-91f3-7f35d3cba561" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139598 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495511 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495511 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495511 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "00b2500b-de4f-55ca-a5fe-606c9cc41191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495535 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{in}}{\\text{s}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495535 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495535 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a31c016-7581-51c5-822b-4a571829ce10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495541 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{kg}}{{\\text{cow}}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495541 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495541 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d10ee8f-e8d6-56f3-a936-711052259f70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495572 #edb/ref 1080 "Pants per sewing machine" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495572 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495572 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1db72ead-e219-506e-a05e-8d12d99ca06d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495607 #edb/ref 1080 "Sewing machines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495607 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495607 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2bc1cc65-cce6-5aab-a972-6c9fe588281f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495640 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{cow}}{{\\text{kg}}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495640 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 1759218604541